      "problem": "Find $a$ if $-2$ is a root of ${x}^{4}+a{x}^{3}-11{x}^{2}+60x+100.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since  $x=-2$ is a root, we have $f(-2)=0.$ Therefore, we can evaluate the polynomial at $x=-2,$ set it equal to $0,$ and solve the equation for the parameter $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{4}+a(-2)^{3}-11(-2)^{2}+60(-2)+100 & =0 \\\\ 16-8a-44-120+100 & =0 \\\\ -8a-48 & =0 \\\\ -8a & =48 \\\\ a & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
